commit 64c18a24126f785c8532c9ba4ddb35ff8a6fc6f1
Author: evisdren <evis@entire.io>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 11:39:42 2026 -0800

    fix(status): drift-aware seed freshness for shared multi-worktree brains

    One brain is keyed by the origin remote and shared by every worktree of
    the repo, so `seed commit != HEAD` is the permanent state of all but one
    worktree; the strict equality check made "seed is stale; run refresh"
    permanent noise, and running refresh only moved the noise to a different
    worktree (COR-2315).

    The seed axis now classifies the drift with one git call
    (`rev-list --count --left-right seed...HEAD`): within 50 commits on one
    line of history reads ok with a "built from <sha>, N commit(s)
    behind/ahead" detail; divergence, larger distance, or an unreadable
    comparison keeps the stale verdict. Refresh's own rebuild decision is
    unchanged — an explicit refresh still rebuilds on any mismatch.

    COR-2315

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M73FJCP8YK45J1QDCTM58BBK

